course: dictionary
lesson: 7776
title: Puzzle: a game, a mystery, a puzzled mind
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A puzzle can be a thing you play with, like a jigsaw with many pieces, a crossword or a riddle. A puzzle can also be something hard to understand, like «Where the cat went is a puzzle».
explain: Puzzle is also a verb. To puzzle someone is to make them wonder or feel confused. «The detective was puzzled by the footprints» means the footprints made the detective think hard, because at first they did not make sense.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. Ask yourself: is someone playing a game, or is someone confused? Look at the words around puzzle, such as pieces, solve, clues or footprints.
fact: A puzzle (noun) is a game or problem you solve by thinking.
fact: «Puzzle» can also mean something hard to understand.
fact: «To puzzle» (verb) means to make someone wonder or feel confused.
fact: «To puzzle over» something means to think hard about it.
fact: Puzzles, puzzles, puzzled and puzzling are all forms of the same word.
exercise: In «Read every word, find the one fact that cracks the puzzle», what does puzzle mean? | A small pet | A kind of bread | *A problem you solve by thinking | A loud noise
exercise: «The detective was puzzled by the footprints.» What does puzzled mean? | Very happy | Angry and shouting | *Confused and wondering | Quickly running away
exercise: Which of these is a puzzle you could do with pieces? | A sunny day | A running race | A glass of water | *A jigsaw
test: Mia sat on the floor to finish her crossword, and she was puzzling over the last clue. What does puzzling over mean? | *Thinking hard about it | Forgetting it completely | Shouting the answer | Drawing a picture
test: «Where the cat went is a puzzle.» What does puzzle mean here? | *Something hard to understand | A kind of pet | A game with pieces | A loud noise
exam: The clues were hard, and they left Sam ___ for hours. Which word fits best? | *puzzled | puzzling | puzzles | puzzle
